      "mergedPostDetails": "New issue noticed from last night that occurs with various setups of 3 point/FBT and does not occur when switching back to the current live steam build. My avatar is not properly reflecting the movement or rotation horizontally/vertically of my headset. From my POV, tracking works fine and there is no issues, but what others see and what I see in a mirror/face mirror is only half the movement of what my IRL movement is\n\nIE: Standing straight up with FBT, moving my head 90 degrees to the left horizontally, my avatars head will only reflect about 45 degrees of that movement. Occurs as well with vertical rotation\n\nSetup\n\nI use a PCVR connected QuestPro with HTC base stations and 6  Vive 3.0 trackers where 1 is a unicorn tracker used to continuously calibrate steam to quest playspaces, and am on the beta branch by default\n\nTroubling performed so far:\n\nRestarted VRChat\n\nRestarted SteamVR\n\nRestarted QuestPro\n\nRestarted PC\n\nRestarted Playspace Calibrator\n\nTested Full body hip lock, head lock, or both lock\n\n(In head lock/both lock specifically, the head movement of the avatar reflects about 10% of actual IRL movement instead of 50% with hip lock. All other testing done on hip lock except 3pointing [obviously])\n\nTested in 3 point with all native quest pro controllers so no steamVR playspace calibration issues (this resulted in a near permanent downward angle tilt of my avatars head. This more or less confirms it to not be a playspace calibration issue)\n\nMultiple restarts again after\n\nNo one else seemed to have the same issue as me in my instances last night who also owned either a Pro or a 3 (all using PCVR as well with FBT)\n\nQuick recording showing the issue. Most noticeable when rotating head up or to the right. Tracking clearly working on my POV but avatar doesn't reflect. Happens on multiple avatars as well. I have not updated any of the avatars since the issue started",
      "mergedPostTitle": "When moving or rotating my head, my in game avatar only reflects half of the movement despite my POV and tracking having no issues reflecting IRL rotation",
